  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Aptos is a Layer 1 proof-of-stake blockchain platform founded in 2022 by former Diem (Meta) engineers, designed for safety, scalability, and high throughput. It employs the Move programming language \u2014 a resource-oriented, formally verifiable language originally created for the Diem project \u2014 to express accounts, digital assets, and smart contracts. Its primary performance innovation is Block-STM (Software Transactional Memory), a parallel transaction execution engine that speculatively executes transactions and resolves conflicts at runtime, enabling high concurrent throughput without requiring developers to pre-declare access sets. The network uses a Byzantine Fault Tolerant consensus mechanism (AptosBFT, derived from HotStuff) to reach finality with low latency.",
